# Delegation

¶ - Briefing contract and error escalation. Routed from the global policy ¶5; read before the first spawn of a session.

document:
  id: taks.delegation@1
  version: 1
  status: proposed
  authority_basis: [@taks/global-policy]
  scope: briefing, escalation
  excludes: inline_vs_spawn_decision # global policy owns it

¶ 1 — Briefing Contract

```text
language TDSL, pure # overrides the harness push toward prose briefings
required [explicit_paths functional_spec validation_criteria constraints minimal_technical_context]
briefing_misses_any_required -> abort_spawn, refine_spec

economy briefing is resent every turn × every subagent -> keep it minimal
rule point to the artifact file; the agent reads it once
rule key_files are path plus a one-line role, nothing deeper
rule deep detail lives in the spec, never inlined in the briefing
ban mandating scoped reads # drives a tool-call storm and inflates cost
target <~400 tokens
template {{KERNEL_HOME}}/templates/briefing.template
```

¶ 2 — Escalation

```text
1 analyze executor return
2 ambiguous_briefing -> clarify_briefing, reopen_same_executor
3 underestimated_complexity -> upgrade_model_tier, new_briefing
4 insufficient_context -> research inline or spawn a research agent, retry
5 fail_persists(2_attempts) -> freeze, report(operator)

rate_limit -> scale_if_permitted, pause_and_report(operator)
unexpected_complexity -> executor_signals_escalation
```

¶ 3 — Return Handling

```text
executor_claims_success -> verify against the validation criteria, never take it at face value
executor_contradicts_prior_finding -> re-derive from code before accepting the correction
```
